❌ **Closed — not a bug. The premise was wrong.**

No code change. The placeholder `e.g., MA-2024-001234` is **accurate**: the system really does generate order numbers in that format today.

```ts
// packages/api/src/routes/orders.ts:47
const ORDER_NUMBER_PREFIX = "MA";
// packages/api/src/routes/admin/orders.ts:50
const ORDER_NUMBER_PREFIX = "MA";
```

`generateOrderNumber()` emits `MA-YYYY-NNNNNN`. I filed this ticket assuming the string was rebrand leftover; it is the **order-number scheme itself** that still carries the masonart prefix. The ticket did hedge this ("if orders really are still prefixed MA-, raise that separately — it is a bigger rebrand gap"), and that is what happened.

**Why I did not just change the prefix**: it is a one-line edit with real consequences and it is a product/ops decision, not a bug fix — historical orders are `MA-`, customers hold those numbers in emails and tracking links, and admin lookup keys off the prefix in four places. Changing the constant would silently break lookup of every existing order.

Raised as **#361** for a decision. Closing this one as invalid.

Also checked while here: no other user-facing `masonart` strings remain.

