ticket.description:
## The bug

`packages/web/app/routes/_authed/account/index.tsx:154-164`'s `handleSignOut` used to wrap `signOut()` in `try/catch`. During the recent server-cart-write-path work it became `try/finally`:

```ts
const handleSignOut = async () => {
  try {
    await signOut()
  } finally {
    // Whether or not the request came back cleanly, this browser is done
    // showing this account's cart...
    onSignedOut()
    navigate({ to: '/' })
  }
}
```

A `signOut()` rejection now propagates out of `handleSignOut` as an unhandled promise rejection instead of being caught and logged. The `finally` block still runs — `onSignedOut()` clears the local cart and `navigate({ to: '/' })` still fires — so there is no user-visible regression; the browser still ends up signed out and redirected either way.

`packages/web/app/components/admin/AdminSidebar.tsx:179-192` was touched by the same piece of work and kept its `catch`:

```ts
const handleSignOut = async () => {
  try {
    await signOut()
  } catch (error) {
    // Surface the failure instead of silently redirecting with a live
    // session — that's exactly how #341 stayed invisible.
    console.error('Sign out failed:', error)
  }
  clearLocalCart()
  window.location.href = '/'
}
```

So the two sign-out paths in the app now disagree on how a failed sign-out is reported: the admin path logs it (per the explicit #341 rationale in its own comment — a hand-rolled body-less fetch once 500'd through the prod edge and left a session alive undetected), the account path does not.

## Why this matters, and why it's low priority

Nothing is user-visibly broken — both paths still clear local state and navigate away. The risk is purely diagnostic: a `signOut()` failure on the account page (network blip, 500 from Better Auth, the same class of prod-edge issue #341 called out) is invisible — no console log, no telemetry, just a rejected promise the browser swallows. If sessions ever fail to sign out silently in production, the admin path would show it and the account path would not.

## Suggested fix

Restore `try/catch` (with the same `console.error` treatment `AdminSidebar.tsx` uses, or shared telemetry) around `signOut()` in `handleSignOut`, keeping `onSignedOut()` and `navigate({ to: '/' })` running unconditionally afterward — i.e. `try/catch` followed by the cleanup, not `try/catch/finally` folding the cleanup into `catch` only. A regression test should assert that a rejected `signOut()` is caught (logged, not thrown) and that the cart is still cleared and navigation still happens.

## Found while

Final review of the server-cart-authoritative change (ticket #511 follow-on), 2026-08-06/07. Not fixed as part of that review — filed instead, per instruction to only fix the cart pricing residual.

